    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0275" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.515/546</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Administrator of the Foreign Economic
                        Administration</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Crowley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-06">March 6, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Leo</hi>: With reference to my letter of
                    February 17 on Indian silver, I am enclosing herewith a copy of a letter from
                    Lord Halifax, dated February 29<anchor n="53" xml:id="d271-f1"/> requesting
                    reconsideration of the decision regarding the guarantee for the return of the
                    100,000,000 ounces of silver for use in India. You will note that he requests
                    immediate shipment of 10,000,000 ounces without prejudice to the larger
                    question.</p>
                <p>I have told Lord Halifax that we shall review carefully the decision regarding
                    guarantees and that in the meantime I felt it would be possible to ship the
                    10,000,000 ounces without prejudicing the final decision, and with the
                    understanding that the decision on the guarantee for the remaining 90,000,000
                    ounces will also apply to the emergency shipment of 10,000,000 ounces.</p>
                <p>With the understanding outlined above, I would appreciate it if you would consult
                    with your administration and Treasury Department in order to determine the
                    manner in which the 10,000,000 ounce shipment should be temporarily
                    documented.</p>
                <p>With best wishes,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
